    "newMechanics": [],
    "solution": "Send the broad stone down the low delivery tunnel, then follow on foot beneath the light. Pass the still-empty casting frame before striking it from the vault side. The permanent cast now blocks the light that prevented jumping around the delivered stone, as well as establishing its return stop. Reach the far side, collect the tally, and dash into the stone from its right. It parks beneath the hanging climb. Jump and dash up the nearby wall, climb-jump onto its visible cap, then jump and dash the open gap to the raised exit.",
    "nearestExisting": "n2 Bell Stop positions a slide stone against an existing stopper; p109 Cold Cast creates a landing. Here the necessary stopper must be absent during the outbound delivery and manufactured for the returning stone. Casting first traps the stone in the low tunnel before the vault.",
    "novelty": "The cast is both a replacement beam shield and an accurately placed return stop. It must stay open for the stone AND the knight to pass before it is closed. The first stop no longer has a climbable lip at jumping height. This replaces a largely linear out-and-back with a visible change in which movements are safe.",
